 "notes": "Curve is the black Rice95 95% C.L. upper limit for the equilibrium halo model (bottom panel of Fig. 5, file fig5cmerged.pdf in the e-print), recovered from the vector paths and calibrated against the axis major ticks. The paper quotes the limit as C_e/F_a in PeV^-1 (Eq. 3 wind Hamiltonian H = C_e a0_tilde/(2F_a) sin(...) v_a.sigma/c, the standard L = (C_e/2f_a) d_mu a ebar gamma^mu gamma5 e convention); converted via g_ae = m_e * C_e/F_a = (C_e/F_a in PeV^-1) x 5.11e-10. Plateau g_ae ~ 3e-10 corresponds to the abstract's F_a/C_e > 2e15 eV. Paper assumes rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (same as canonical, no rescaling) and |v_a| = 240 km/s. Panels a/b of Fig. 5 show direction-dependent stream-scenario exclusions (v_a along X or Y); the equilibrium-model curve is reported as the main result. Raw 478-segment curve resampled to 100 log-spaced points; jagged fine structure (Rayleigh noise, averaged above 2 zeV by the authors) is smoothed accordingly.",
